description:
Please act as a professional Verilog designer.

Design a module that implements an 8-bit shift register with parallel load and shift left capabilities. The shift register can either load an 8-bit value in parallel or shift its bits to the left on each rising edge of the clock based on a control signal.

Module name:
    shift_register

Input ports:
    clk: Clock signal used for synchronous operation.
    reset: Synchronous reset signal.
    load: Control signal to load data in parallel.
    data_in: 8-bit input data to be loaded into the shift register.
    shift_in: Serial input data for the shift operation.

Output ports:
    q: 8-bit output signal representing the shift register value.

Implementation:
The output q is defined as reg [7:0] q and initialized to 8'b00000000 using the initial statement. The value of q is updated on the rising edge of the clock: if (load) q <= data_in; else q <= {q[6:0], shift_in}.
If the reset signal is high, q is reset to 8'b00000000: if (reset) q <= 8'b00000000.

Give me the complete code.

module shift_register(clk, reset, load, data_in, shift_in, q);

    input clk;
    input reset;
    input load;
    input [7:0] data_in;
    input shift_in;
    output [7:0] q;

code:
module shift_register(clk, reset, load, data_in, shift_in, q);

    input clk;
    input reset;
    input load;
    input [7:0] data_in;
    input shift_in;
    output [7:0] q;
    reg [7:0] q;
    initial q = 8'b00000000;

    always @(posedge clk)
        begin
            if (reset)
                q <= 8'b00000000;
            else if (load)
                q <= data_in;
            else
                q <= {q[6:0], shift_in};
        end

endmodule

