description:
Design a Johnson counter with a specified number of flip-flops, defined by the parameter n. On each positive clock edge, the counter generates a new state by shifting the current state to the left while inserting the inverted value of the most significant bit at the least significant position. The resulting state is output as a binary vector, effectively cycling through a unique sequence of states based on the counter's configuration.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg [n-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg [n-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of flip-flops

reg [n-1:0] state;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  state <= {state[n-2:0], ~state[n-1]};
  out <= state;
end

endmodule

