description:
Develop a relaxation ring oscillator with adjustable frequency modulation based on a capacitor charging and discharging mechanism. The module consists of a series of inverters forming a ring oscillator that operates at a clock signal. It incorporates a relaxation oscillator that modulates the frequency of the ring oscillator depending on the voltage across a capacitor compared to a computed threshold. The output is derived from the last inverter in the ring, producing an oscillating signal whose frequency can be varied by altering the capacitor's charge state. This design serves to generate a variable frequency clock signal suitable for various timing applications.
