description:
Design a module that performs a series of bitwise and arithmetic operations on two 8-bit input vectors. It first computes the bitwise AND and OR of the inputs, then adds the results of these operations together. Additionally, it calculates the bitwise XOR of the AND and OR results and increments this value by one. Finally, the module outputs the result of this final addition as an 8-bit vector. This design illustrates a combination of logical and arithmetic functions which can be useful in digital signal processing or computational logic applications.
module top_module(
    input [7:0] in1,
    input [7:0] in2,
    output reg [7:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [7:0] in1,
    input [7:0] in2,
    output reg [7:0] out
);// Step 1: Compute the bitwise AND of in1 and in2
    wire [7:0] and_result = in1 & in2;

    // Step 2: Compute the bitwise OR of in1 and in2
    wire [7:0] or_result = in1 | in2;

    // Step 3: Add the results of step 1 and step 2
    wire [8:0] add_result = and_result + or_result;

    // Step 4: Compute the bitwise XOR of the results of step 1 and step 2
    wire [7:0] xor_result = and_result ^ or_result;

    // Step 5: Add 1 to the result of step 4
    wire [7:0] add_one = 1;
    wire [7:0] add_one_result = xor_result + add_one;

    // Step 6: Assign the result of step 5 to out
    always @(*) begin
        out = add_one_result;
    end

endmodule

