Implement a circuit that converts a 4-bit Gray code input into its equivalent binary representation. The most significant bit of the binary output directly reflects the most significant bit of the Gray code input, while the remaining bits are derived through exclusive OR (XOR) operations involving the higher bits of the Gray code.
module top_module(input [3:0] G, 
         output [3:0] bin   
        );

code:
module top_module(input [3:0] G, 
         output [3:0] bin   
        );assign bin[3] = G[3];
assign bin[2] = G[3] ^ G[2];
assign bin[1] = G[3] ^ G[2] ^ G[1];
assign bin[0] = G[3] ^ G[2] ^ G[1] ^ G[0];endmodule

