description:
Design a one-shot pulse generator that produces a single output pulse in response to a trigger signal. The pulse duration, defined in clock cycles, can be configured with a parameter. Upon receiving a trigger signal, the output pulse is set HIGH, and a counter begins counting clock cycles. Once the counter reaches the specified pulse duration, the output pulse transitions back to LOW. The module effectively ensures that a brief, controlled pulse is generated on triggering while maintaining the ability to define the pulse length.
module top_module(
  input clk,          // Added clk input signal
  input trigger,
  output pulse
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,          // Added clk input signal
  input trigger,
  output pulse
);parameter pulse_duration = 10; // duration of output pulse in clock cycles

reg [7:0] counter;
reg pulse_state;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (trigger) begin
    counter <= 0;
    pulse_state <= 1;
  end else if (pulse_state) begin
    counter <= counter + 1;
    if (counter >= pulse_duration) begin
      pulse_state <= 0;
    end
  end
end

assign pulse = pulse_state;

endmodule

