Design a 16x16 array multiplier that takes two 16-bit inputs, A and B, and produces a 32-bit output representing their product. The implementation utilizes a generate statement to create a series of row-wise partial products by multiplying each bit of A with the entire B input, then combines these results through bit-shifting and addition into the final output using another generate block. This design efficiently computes the multiplication using parallel processing, characteristic of array multiplier architectures.
