Develop a 4-to-8 binary encoder that converts a 4-bit input digit (0-9) into its corresponding 8-bit encoded output to represent the digit in a 7-segment display format. Each input value maps to a specific byte (in hexadecimal) that controls which segments of the display are illuminated, with an output of 8'hFF for invalid inputs.
module top_module(
		input [3 : 0] digit,
		output reg [7 : 0] encoding
	);

