Design a BCD encoder that converts an 8-bit binary input representing a decimal value into its Binary-Coded Decimal (BCD) representation. The module produces two 4-bit outputs: "BCD_decade" representing the ten's place and "BCD_unit" representing the unit's place of the input decimal value. The BCD_decade is derived from dividing the input by 10 and taking the remainder of that result, while the BCD_unit is obtained by calculating the modulus of the input with 10.
