description:
Design a circuit that implements a delay line for a single-bit input signal. The circuit uses a shift register to introduce a specified delay of 4 clock cycles, where the input signal is shifted through the register with each clock edge. The output produces the value of the input signal as it was 4 clock cycles prior, effectively serving as a delay buffer for digital signals.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input in,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input in,
  output out
);parameter delay = 4; // delay in clock cycles

// shift register to delay input signal
reg [delay-1:0] shift_reg;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  shift_reg <= {shift_reg[delay-2:0], in};
end

assign out = shift_reg[delay-1];

endmodule

